        "procedure": "A degassed deep-purple THF solution of Sm(OTf)2(dme)2 was reacted with N2O. The solution discolored completely in approximately 15 h and a white precipitate formed. Filtration and slow evaporation gave 1 in 85% yield. X-ray-quality crystals were grown by slow diffusion of pentane into a THF solution. A low amount of O2 in THF also caused the purple solution to fade, and storage of the colorless solution at −35 °C afforded a few crystals of 1; the yield of that route could not be calculated. Reaction with one atmosphere of dry O2 was not clean.",
